# Hackelwurfkapelle, back-layer prop: an open wayside chapel (whitewashed
# w front, i shade, a big round arch with a d back wall and i reveal, a
# shingle gable O/o/l) with the stone figure of St. Wolfgang (i lit, m
# shade, d folds) on an i/m pedestal: bishop's mitre, crozier with its curl
# in the left hand, the right arm raised high throwing his Hackl: a 1 px m
# handle diagonal (5 px) from the hand up to a 4x4 i blade with an m
# lower-right edge and a w glint at its top left. His mitre top (the pigeon's
# seat) is the mitre tip at sprite (22, 24): 2 px left of the origin, 40 px
# above it. No outline (back layer). Drawn by the pixel-artist with a
# throwaway script; the grid is the source.
sprite = hackelwurfkapelle
size   = 48x64
origin = 24,64
anim   = idle frames=1
